Seam: AddAboutStrings in
      chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc,
      where the About page's text is made.
Why: two things the page could not say for itself. It named Chromium's
     version alone, so a reader reporting a problem, or checking that an
     update took, saw nothing that told two Kyuzen releases on the same
     Chromium apart; it now leads with Kyuzen's version and build number. And
     the update setting's row needs a label and three choices, which the
     browser builds from the setting's own values so that the row and the
     browser cannot come to disagree about what was chosen.

     Both are taken here, in one patch, because two patches adding lines to
     the same part of a file cannot afterwards be told apart from a conflict.
Delegates to: arcium/common/product_version.cc (arcium::AboutVersionText) and
     arcium/ui/browser/update_settings.cc (arcium::AddUpdateSettingStrings).
     The GN deps both need are in patch 0191.

